3:T507,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"LocalBusiness","name":"Boots Opticians Lincoln","description":"Boots Opticians is one of the UK's largest and most recognised optical chains, operating from Boots pharmacy stores across the country. They offer a full range of eye care services including NHS and private eye tests, designer and own-brand glasses, contact lenses, and hearing care. With their convenient high-street locations and integration with Boots Advantage Card loyalty points, they remain a popular choice for routine eye care.","url":"https://www.eyetest.co.uk/opticians/boots-opticians/lincoln","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Lincoln","addressRegion":"Lincolnshire","addressCountry":"GB","postalCode":"LN1 3BH"},"geo":{"@type":"GeoCoordinates","latitude":53.2307,"longitude":-0.5406},"parentOrganization":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Boots Opticians","url":"https://www.boots-opticians.co.uk"},"priceRange":"Free NHS / From £25 private","openingHoursSpecification":[{"@type":"OpeningHoursSpecification","dayOfWeek":["Monday","Tuesday","Wednesday","Thursday","Friday"],"opens":"09:00","closes":"17:30"},{"@type":"OpeningHoursSpecification","dayOfWeek":"Saturday","opens":"09:00","closes":"17:00"}],"areaServed":{"@type":"City","name":"Lincoln"}}4:Ted2,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does an eye test cost at Boots in Lincoln?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Boots eye tests in Lincoln are priced at Free NHS / From £25 private. Many patients qualify for free NHS-funded eye tests. You can compare prices and book online through eyetest.co.uk."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I get a free NHS eye test at Boots in Lincoln?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, Boots in Lincoln offers NHS-funded eye tests for eligible patients. Eligibility includes being under 16, over 60, on certain benefits, or having specific medical conditions. In Scotland, all residents qualify for free NHS eye tests regardless of age or income."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I book an eye test at Boots Lincoln?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"You can book a Boots eye test in Lincoln by entering the postcode LN1 3BH on eyetest.co.uk. You will see available appointment slots, compare prices, and book online instantly. You can also call your local Boots branch directly."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How long does an eye test take at Boots?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A standard eye test at Boots typically takes between 20 and 30 minutes. If you opt for an enhanced test with OCT scanning, allow around 35 to 45 minutes. Contact lens consultations may take 30 to 45 minutes as they involve additional measurements and a trial fitting."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I need to bring anything to my eye test at Boots?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, bring your current glasses or contact lenses, any NHS exemption evidence if you qualify for a free test, and a list of any medications you take. If you have a previous prescription from another optician, bringing that along can be helpful for comparison."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What happens if I need glasses after my Boots eye test?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"After your eye test at Boots in Lincoln, your optometrist will provide a written prescription. You can choose glasses from Boots's range, or take your prescription to any other optician. If you qualify for an NHS optical voucher, this can be put towards the cost of your glasses."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can children have eye tests at Boots in Lincoln?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, Boots in Lincoln offers eye tests for children of all ages. All children under 16 are entitled to free NHS-funded eye tests. Boots optometrists use age-appropriate techniques including picture charts and matching games for younger children who cannot yet read letters."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How often should I have an eye test?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The recommended frequency is every two years for most adults. However, you should have annual eye tests if you are over 70, have diabetes, have a family history of glaucoma, or have been advised by your optometrist. Children should have their eyes tested annually. Book your next eye test at Boots in Lincoln through eyetest.co.uk."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What services does Boots offer in Lincoln?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Boots in Lincoln offers: NHS Eye Tests, Private Eye Tests, Contact Lenses, Glasses, Hearing Tests, Children's Eye Tests, OCT Scan, Diabetic Screening. Book your appointment through eyetest.co.uk to check real-time availability."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are there other opticians near Boots in Lincoln?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, there are 8 other opticians available to book in Lincoln, including ASDA Opticians, Leightons Opticians & Hearing Care, Rawlings Opticians. Compare them all on eyetest.co.uk."}}]}0:{"rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[[["$","$L2",null,{}],["$","main",null,{"className":"flex-1","children":[["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Home\",\"item\":\"https://www.eyetest.co.uk\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"Opticians\",\"item\":\"https://www.eyetest.co.uk/opticians\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":3,\"name\":\"Boots Opticians\",\"item\":\"https://www.eyetest.co.uk/opticians/boots-opticians\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":4,\"name\":\"Lincoln\",\"item\":\"https://www.eyetest.co.uk/opticians/boots-opticians/lincoln\"}]}"}}],["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$3"}}],["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","